*** MISSING >> Helpful NullPointerExceptions (JEP 358, Java 14+, ON by default) - relevant to whole Exception Format section above
    >> before Java 14, NPE message was just:
       Exception in thread "main" java.lang.NullPointerException
    >> Java 14+ gives a PRECISE description of exactly which variable/field/method call was null:
       Exception in thread "main" java.lang.NullPointerException:
           Cannot invoke "String.length()" because "s" is null
             	at org.example.exception_handling.ExceptionVsError.main(ExceptionVsError.java:17)
    >> huge debugging improvement - pinpoints WHICH reference in a chained call (a.b.c.d()) was null
    >> enabled by default from Java 15 onwards (JVM flag -XX:+ShowCodeDetailsInExceptionMessages needed pre-15)

