*** MISSING >>
Records + Exceptions (Java 16+, standard in 17) - relevant new exception-raising pattern
    record Employee(int id, String name){
        Employee {                              // compact constructor
            if(id < 0)
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("id cannot be negative");   // #7 above, raised explicitly
        }
    }
    >> compact constructor is the recommended place to validate record components
       and throw IllegalArgumentException / NullPointerException(Java 14+ style) proactively,
       BEFORE fields get assigned

*** MISSING >>
Sealed Classes + Custom Exception hierarchies (Java 17) - design-level addition
    sealed class AppException extends Exception permits ValidationException, DbException {}
    final class ValidationException extends AppException {}
    final class DbException extends AppException {}
    >> lets you define a CLOSED set of custom exception types
    >> useful for catch-block exhaustiveness reasoning - compiler/reviewer knows
       there are NO other possible subtypes of AppException outside this file/module
    >> combine with good-practice catch ordering (child >> child >> parent) shown above -
       now the "child" list is guaranteed complete, nothing can sneak in later unnoticed

